==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} {{term|Huguenot||Huguenot; also, a personal name and surname|lang=fr}}, diminutive of {{term|Hugo|lang=fr}}, {{term|Hugon|lang=fr}}, {{term|Hugues|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|gmh}} {{term|Hug|Hūg|lang=gmh}}, {{term|Huc|Hūc|Hugh, a man's name|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|gmh}} {{term|huge||mind|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh}} {{term|hugu||mind, thought|lang=goh}}, from {{proto|Germanic|huguz||hugiz|mind|lang=en}}, of unknown origin. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|hyge||thought, mind, heart, disposition, intention, courage, pride|lang=ang}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|hyū'gə-nŏt'}}, {{IPA|/ˈhju.ɡən.ɒt/}}

===Noun===
